{"name":"Kid Icarus","hex":"#a81000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Koshin."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A child, adolescent, or  a young adult.","A person whose childhood took place in a particular time period or area."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kid Icarus","blocks":[{"text":"Kid Icarus is a 1986 action-platform game developed and published by Nintendo for the Family Computer Disk System in Japan and the Nintendo Entertainment System in Europe and North America. It was released in Japan in December 1986, in Europe in February 1987, and in North America in July."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b1/Kid_Icarus_NES_box_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid_Icarus","wikidata":"Q1142493"},{"title":"Kid Icarus (series)","blocks":[{"text":"Kid Icarus is a series of fantasy video games by Nintendo. Set in the fantasy world of \"Angel Land\", which is loosely based on Greco-Roman mythology, the gameplay combines action, adventure and platforming elements. The Kid Icarus franchise is known as a cult classic and a sibling series to the Metroid franchise."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Kid_Icarus_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid_Icarus_(series)","wikidata":"Q1740851"},{"title":"Icarus","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Icarus was the son of the master craftsman Daedalus, the architect of the labyrinth of Crete, and his wife Naucrate. After Theseus, king of Athens and enemy of King Minos, escaped from the labyrinth, Minos suspected that Icarus and Daedalus had revealed the labyrinth's secrets and thus imprisoned the two, either in a large tower overlooking the ocean or in the labyrinth itself, depending upon the account."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1873.jpg/330px-Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1873.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icarus","wikidata":"Q34041"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/88/Kid_Icarus_Sky_World.png/250px-Kid_Icarus_Sky_World.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/88/Kid_Icarus_Sky_World.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/88/Kid_Icarus_Sky_World.png/250px-Kid_Icarus_Sky_World.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pit fights the monsters of the game with a bow and arrow. The player character's health and the number of hearts is displayed in the top-left corner of the screen. Doors in levels lead to different chambers, such as treasuries or item stores.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKid_Icarus_Sky_World.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Kid_Icarus_major_characters.png/330px-Kid_Icarus_major_characters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Kid_Icarus_major_characters.png/330px-Kid_Icarus_major_characters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pit (top-left), Palutena (top-right), Dark Pit (bottom-left), and Medusa (bottom-right) serve as important characters narratively.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKid_Icarus_major_characters.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg/500px-Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg/1280px-Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg/500px-Gowy-icaro-prado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jacob Peter Gowy's The Fall of Icarus (1635–1637)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGowy-icaro-prado.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg/250px-Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg/500px-Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg/250px-Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Daedalus_mosaic_1871.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg/250px-At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg/500px-At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg/250px-At_Tenerife_2021_0099.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAt_Tenerife_2021_00